    "text_frames": [
      {
        "id": "notes",
        "position": [
          2,
          1
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**CT04 \u2014 Does integral action remove the load error?**  \n**Predict \u2192 Run \u2192 Inspect \u2192 Change one thing.** Run 16 s at 100 Hz. Reference 0 \u2192 0.5 at 1 s; opposing load 0 \u2192 0.2 at 8 s.  \nPredict P equilibrium 1/3 before load and 4/15 after it. PI/PID return toward 0.5. All units are normalized (1).  \nOpen the three Scopes. Select kd, F4: value 0.15 \u2192 0; save/reopen/rerun. PID should become PI, not a better controller by definition.  \nSource/state index n is observed at Scope time (n+1)/100 s. States update afterward; no extra feedback delay is needed.  \n[Open CT04 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/CT04-controller-comparison/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT PID lecture](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/16-06-principles-of-automatic-control-fall-2012/resources/mit16_06f12_lecture_10/) \u00b7 [MIT windup notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-017j-design-of-electromechanical-robotic-systems-fall-2009/MIT2_017JF09_feedback.pdf)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1800,
          "height": 400,
          "font_size": 20
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
